---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import Callout from '../../components/Callout.astro';
import '../../styles/rules.css';
import '../../styles/armies.css';
import { accentColor, FACTIONS, FACTION_BLURBS, slug, heroUnit, portrait, unitCount } from '../../lib/factions';
import { ARMY_SIZES } from '../../lib/data';
import { ARMY_BUILDER_URL, url } from '../../lib/site';
import builderShot from '../../assets/site/army-builder.jpg';
---
<Base title="Building an Army" description="How to build a SOVL army - army sizes, points, sections, commanders and retinues - and the army lists of every faction." section="Armies">
  <div class="armies">
    <header class="armies-hero">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Armies</p>
        <h1>Building an Army</h1>
        <p class="lede">Pick a faction, agree on a size, and spend your points. Every army list is below, and you can build yours right now in the browser.</p>
        <div class="faction-cta">
          <a class="btn btn-gold" href={ARMY_BUILDER_URL}>Open the Army Builder</a>
          <a class="btn" href="#factions">Browse the factions</a>
        </div>
      </div>
      <Image class="armies-hero-shot" src={builderShot} alt="The SOVL Army Builder showing a Knights of Avalon army with a commander's unit card." width={900} widths={[480, 900]} sizes="(max-width: 900px) 100vw, 50vw" loading="eager" />
    </header>

    <section class="prose armies-rules">
      <h2 id="army-size">Army size</h2>
      <p>Before a battle, both players agree on an <strong>army size</strong>. It sets your points limit and the most units you can bring.</p>
      <div class="size-cards">
        {ARMY_SIZES.map((s) => (
          <div class="size-card">
            <span class="size-name">{s.name}</span>
            <span class="size-points">{s.points}<small> pts</small></span>
            <span class="size-units">up to {s.maxUnits} units</span>
          </div>
        ))}
      </div>
      <p>A Warband is a quick skirmish, and a Battalion is a full battle. Unit sizes and section limits grow with the army size, so the same faction can feel quite different at each size.</p>

      <h2 id="sections">Sections</h2>
      <p>Every faction's list is split into <strong>sections</strong>. All factions have <strong>Commanders</strong> and <strong>Battle Line</strong>. The rest are the faction's own: <em>Ranged Support</em>, <em>Fast Attack</em>, <em>Machines of War</em>, <em>Jungle Beasts</em> and so on.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>Each section has a <strong>minimum</strong> and <strong>maximum</strong> number of units for each army size. Most armies must take at least one commander and some Battle Line.</li>
        <li>A few units count as <strong>half</strong> a unit, or as <strong>two</strong>, against their section's limits. Their cards say so.</li>
        <li>Some units can only be taken a limited number of times per army. Their cards show <em>Max per army</em>.</li>
        <li>A few commanders raise a section's maximum by one.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="commanders">Commanders and retinues</h2>
      <p>Every army needs at least one <strong>commander</strong>. Larger armies can have more. A commander joins a unit, its <strong>retinue</strong>, chosen from the units listed on its card. Some retinues aren't available in a Warband.</p>
      <ul>
        <li>A commander and its retinue are <strong>one unit</strong> on the battlefield and in your unit count. You pay for both.</li>
        <li>The retinue counts towards its own section's <em>minimum</em>, but not its <em>maximum</em>.</li>
        <li>Some commanders ride a <strong>mount</strong> instead: a monster, chariot or war beast from the faction's Mounts section. A few are monsters themselves and fight alone.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 id="options">Options and magic</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Equipment choices</strong>: many units choose between weapon sets, or buy upgrades. An upgrade's cost is per model unless it says per unit.</li>
        <li><strong>Spellcasters</strong> choose one cantrip and one major spell from their list.</li>
        <li><strong>Magic items</strong>: most commanders can carry a magic weapon or item, and some units can carry a magic banner. See the <a href={url('/reference/glossary/#magic-items')}>magic items</a>.</li>
        <li><strong>Unit size and width</strong>: regiments choose how many models to field, within the limits for the army size, and how wide their front rank is.</li>
      </ul>
      <Callout type="tip">
        <p>Every faction comes with a ready-made list for each common size, so you can play straight away and tweak it later.</p>
      </Callout>
    </section>

    <section id="factions" class="factions-block">
      <h2>The factions</h2>
      {FACTIONS.length === 0 ? (
        <p class="pending">The army lists are being updated from the latest version of the game. Check back soon, or open the <a href={ARMY_BUILDER_URL}>Army Builder</a> to see every faction now.</p>
      ) : (
        <div class="faction-grid">
          {FACTIONS.map((f) => {
            const hero = heroUnit(f);
            const img = portrait(hero?.image);
            return (
              <a class="faction-card" href={url(`/armies/${slug(f.id)}/`)} style={`--accent:${accentColor(f)}`}>
                {img && <Image class="faction-card-art" src={img} alt="" width={300} widths={[220, 300]} sizes="220px" loading="lazy" />}
                <span class="faction-card-text">
                  <span class="faction-card-name">{f.name}</span>
                  <span class="faction-card-blurb">{FACTION_BLURBS[f.id] ?? ''}</span>
                  <span class="faction-card-meta">{unitCount(f)} units{f.dlc && <span class="dlc">DLC</span>}</span>
                </span>
              </a>
            );
          })}
        </div>
      )}
    </section>
  </div>
</Base>
